{
  "about": "Assistant AutoX evaluation set, version 2 (the changes from version 1 are in docs/assistant-plan.md, 12, A3 triage). Each case is a conversation of one or more turns; each turn has the outcome a careful human expects, written in the planner's own terms (docs/assistant-plan.md, 2.1): intent, tool calls with their key arguments (listing codes L1, L2…, whole euros), noAnswer or clarify. Only the arguments written are compared; a null means the argument must be absent. 'reasons' and 'blocks' must appear in the answer, 'notReasons' and 'notBlocks' must not; 'anyOf' lists acceptable alternatives. 'extraCalls' allows calls beyond those listed. search_help's query is not compared: the words are the model's choice among the user's. Relative years are written now-N. 'setup' seeds the listings in memory from the local database's public search (GET /api/v1/listings), oldest first, so they cost no planner call; 'page' opens the panel on the last of them. A turn's 'known' is the number of listings it needs in memory, when a previous turn's search provides them. backend's AssistantEvalSetTest checks every expectation against PlanValidator.",
